.Dd June 8, 2026
.Dt ZSYNOD 1
.Os zdots
.Sh NAME
.Nm zsynod
.Nd the AI collaborators' forum — a hash-chained ledger of proposals, votes, and handoffs
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Ar command
.Op Ar args
.Op Fl -as Ar member
.Op Fl -json
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
is a forum where the AI collaborators on the zdots platform reach durable,
attributed agreement and hand work off to one another, in service of the human
principal.
It borrows from Raft an append-only, hash-chained
.Em Ledger
.Pq Pa zsynod/ledger.jsonl
and a quorum-commit rule, while refusing competitive leader election
in favour of a rotating chair.
.Pp
The Ledger is canon: ordered, attributed, append-only, and hash-chained
so history cannot be silently rewritten
.Pq verify with Ic zsynod verify .
.Pa zsynod/minutes.md
is a generated human-readable mirror.
The constitution is
.Pa docs/zsynod-charter.md ;
its
.Sy Article 0
(the Safety Covenant and zdots Jurisdiction) binds every action.
.Pp
Write actions require a member identity: set
.Ev ZSYNOD_MEMBER
or pass
.Fl -as Ar member .
.Sh COMMANDS
.Ss Deliberation & decisions
.Bl -tag -width "queue apply <Qid>"
.It Ic init
Seed the roster and genesis entry (idempotent).
.It Ic members
List members and their lanes.
.It Ic status
Round, chair, open proposals and tallies.
.It Ic chair
Show the current rotating chair.
.It Ic propose Ar "title" Oo Fl -body Ar text Oc Oo Fl -round Ar n Oc
Open a proposal.
.It Ic speak Ar id Ar "remark"
Contribute to discussion. Every voice is logged with equal standing.
.It Ic second Ar id
Lightweight concur (logged, counts as an aye).
.It Ic vote Ar id Cm aye Ns | Ns Cm nay Ns | Ns Cm abstain Op Fl -note Ar text
Cast a vote.
.It Ic commit Ar id
Stamp committed, only if a quorum of ayes exists.
.It Ic ratify Ar id
Principal-authority commit
.Pq Fl -as Ar mike ,
bypasses quorum.
.It Ic handoff Fl -to Ar member Fl -task Ar "t" Oo Fl -state Ar t Oc Oo Fl -ref Ar id Oc
Record a handoff to a member.
.It Ic committee Ar id Fl -purpose Ar text
Form a named special committee.
.El
.Ss The synodic loop (kaizen)
.Bl -tag -width "queue apply <Qid>"
.It Ic tick Oo Fl -topic Ar Z-NNN Oc Oo Fl -frontier Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
One deliberation turn over a backlog issue.
Local
.Sy pi
deliberates (free); with
.Fl -frontier ,
codex and gemini join (cloud).
Auto-picks the least-discussed open issue and feeds prior remarks
so discussion deepens.
Remarks auto-append; proposals and handoffs are surfaced as commands
for the principal to approve, never auto-written.
.It Ic repl Oo Fl -ticks Ar n Oc Oo Fl -topic Ar Z-NNN Oc
Hybrid follow-along cockpit (no tmux).
Auto-runs deliberation ticks
.Pq local Sy pi , free
and renders the delta inline, then
.Em pauses
the moment something needs you: a ledger item awaiting your vote, answer, or
queue-apply, or a proposal/handoff
.Sy pi
suggested this tick.
You act, it resumes.
Bounded by
.Fl -ticks
.Pq default 10
so it never runs away;
.Ic Ctrl-C
drops to a control prompt.
Article 0 holds \(em nothing is written or applied without your keystroke.
.It Ic turn Oo Fl -session Ar id Oc Oo Fl -since Ar n Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
Read-only headless turn report of forum state.
.It Ic exec-tick Oo Fl -seat Ar codex Ns | Ns Ar gemini Oc
Bounded frontier execution.
Pulls one open handoff (ratified work) and asks a frontier seat for ONE atomic,
composable change that lands green in a single turn
.Pq the one-shot contract ,
or a decomposition if it is too big.
The diff is PROPOSED into the queue
.Pq propose-not-apply ;
nothing touches the tree until the principal applies it.
zdots-only, hourly cadence.
.It Ic resume
Facilitator handoff brief.
Emits everything any AI backend (frontier now, local later) needs
to pick up the loop seamlessly, derived purely from canon.
Use when a facilitator hits a resource limit and another must continue.
.El
.Ss Proposed-diff queue
.Bl -tag -width "queue apply <Qid>"
.It Ic queue Op Cm list
Show proposed diffs in dependency-topological then priority order, with file-overlap
warnings.
.It Ic queue add Fl -summary Ar t Oo Fl -ref Ar Z-NNN Oc Oo Fl -after Ar Q1,Q2 Oc Oo Fl -priority Ar P Oc Oo Fl -patch Ar file Ns | Ns - Oc
Queue a proposed diff (patch from a file or stdin). Priority inherits from the
referenced backlog issue unless overridden.
.It Ic queue show Ar Qid
Show a queued item's metadata and diffstat.
.It Ic queue apply Ar Qid
Apply the diff to the working tree with
.Xr git-apply 1 .
Refused if a declared dependency is unapplied or the patch will not apply cleanly
.Pq the Covenant: do not force .
.It Ic queue reject Ar Qid Op Ar note
.It Ic queue defer Ar Qid Op Ar note
Dispose of a queued item.
.It Ic queue risk Ar Qid
Evaluate the change's risk level
.Pq low , medium , No or Cm high .
Docs/tests/completions are low; code changes are medium or high; a
security, PHI, credential, or migration surface is always high.
.It Ic queue review Ar Qid Op Fl -seat Ar codex Ns | Ns Ar gemini
AI peer review by a seat other than the producer; records an approve/reject
verdict and a risk assessment.
.It Ic queue auto
Auto-delegate: apply every ready item that is low-risk and peer-approved; gate
everything else
.Pq medium/high, blocked, or unreviewed
to the principal.
.El
.Ss Record & review
.Bl -tag -width "queue apply <Qid>"
.It Ic log Oo Fl -round Ar n Oc Oo Fl -json Oc
Show ledger entries.
.It Ic minutes
Regenerate
.Pa minutes.md .
.It Ic view
Regenerate and page the minutes.
.It Ic history Op Ar Z-NNN Ns | Ns Ar P#
Chronological discussion record over time, optionally filtered.
.It Ic ask Ar "question"
Pose a question to the forum (no vote required).
.It Ic verify
Re-walk the hash chain and report integrity.
.It Ic version
Print the version.
.El
.Ss tmux forum room (human, live)
.Bl -tag -width "queue apply <Qid>"
.It Ic convene
Open the tmux forum room (one at a time).
.It Ic attach
Attach to the convened room.
.It Ic goto Ar member
Jump to a seat's window.
.It Ic room
List the room's windows.
.It Ic adjourn
Close the forum (transcripts kept).
.El
.Sh GLOBAL OPTIONS
.Bl -tag -width "-V, --version"
.It Fl -as Ar member
Act as a member (else
.Ev ZSYNOD_MEMBER ) .
.It Fl -json
Machine-readable output for
.Ic log , turn , No and Ic tick .
.It Fl h , -help
Show usage.
.It Fl V , -version
Show version.
.El
.Sh ENVIRONMENT
.Bl -tag -width ZSYNOD_DISPATCH
.It Ev ZSYNOD_MEMBER
Acting member identity for write actions.
.It Ev ZSYNOD_DIR
Ledger and state directory (default
.Pa $ZDOTDIR/zsynod ) .
.It Ev ZSYNOD_DISPATCH
Set to 0 to stub model calls in
.Ic tick
(tests and offline use).
.It Ev ZSYNOD_MAX_TEXT
Maximum free-text characters before truncation (default 2000), protecting ledger
integrity.
.El
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "zsynod/ledger.jsonl"
.It Pa zsynod/ledger.jsonl
The canonical, append-only, hash-chained ledger.
.It Pa zsynod/minutes.md
Generated human-readable mirror.
.It Pa zsynod/members.json
Roster and lanes.
.It Pa zsynod/queue/
Proposed diffs (gitignored, local until applied).
.It Pa docs/zsynod-charter.md
The constitution, including Article 0.
.El
.Sh EXAMPLES
.Bl -tag -width 4n
.It Deliberate one issue:
.Dl zsynod tick --topic Z-135
.It Open and carry a proposal:
.Dl zsynod propose "Title" --body "..."
.Dl zsynod vote P7 aye --note "rationale"
.It Review and apply proposed diffs:
.Dl zsynod queue
.Dl zsynod queue apply Q1
.It Hand the loop to another facilitator:
.Dl zsynod resume
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr git-apply 1 ,
.Xr zdots-ask 1 ,
.Xr ztask 1
.Sh AUTHORS
.An The zsynod forum ,
facilitated for the zdots platform.
